 
 NHS RTT Waiting Times Database
 Query Report — 10 Business Queries
 Assessment Task 2
 


 
 Q1. Simple SELECT — List all trusts in the London region
 
 Business question: Which NHS trusts operate within the London region?
 This helps regional commissioners identify all providers in their area.

SELECT t.trust_name,
       t.trust_code,
       t.parent_organisation
FROM   Trust t
JOIN   Region r ON t.region_id = r.region_id
WHERE  r.region_name = 'London'
ORDER BY t.trust_name;


 
 Q2. Simple SELECT with filter — All breaching pathways
 
 Business question: Which patient pathways are currently in breach
 of the 18-week RTT standard?
 Identifies pathways where patients have waited beyond the legal target.

SELECT p.pathway_id,
       t.trust_name,
       s.specialty_name,
       p.rtt_part_type,
       p.weeks_waiting,
       p.patient_count
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Trust     t ON p.trust_id     = t.trust_id
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
WHERE  p.is_breach = 1
ORDER BY p.weeks_waiting DESC;


 
 Q3. Aggregate — Total patients waiting per region
 
 Business question: How many patients in total are waiting in each NHS region?
 Gives an overall demand picture for regional planning.

SELECT r.region_name,
       SUM(w.total_waiting) AS total_patients_waiting
FROM   Waiting_List_Snapshot w
JOIN   Trust  t ON w.trust_id  = t.trust_id
JOIN   Region r ON t.region_id = r.region_id
GROUP BY r.region_name
ORDER BY total_patients_waiting DESC;


 
 Q4. GROUP BY — Breach count by specialty
 
 Business question: Which clinical specialties have the highest number
 of breaching pathway records?
 Helps clinical directors prioritise capacity investment.

SELECT s.specialty_name,
       s.department,
       COUNT(*)              AS breach_records,
       SUM(p.patient_count)  AS breach_patient_count
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
WHERE  p.is_breach = 1
GROUP BY s.specialty_name, s.department
ORDER BY breach_patient_count DESC;


 
 Q5. JOIN across 3 tables — Full pathway detail report
 
 Business question: Produce a full audit listing of all patient pathways
 with trust, region, and specialty context.
 Used by performance managers to review the complete dataset.

SELECT p.pathway_id,
       r.region_name,
       t.trust_name,
       s.specialty_name,
       p.rtt_part_type,
       p.weeks_waiting,
       p.patient_count,
       CASE WHEN p.is_breach = 1 THEN 'BREACH' ELSE 'Within target' END AS status
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Trust     t ON p.trust_id     = t.trust_id
JOIN   Region    r ON t.region_id    = r.region_id
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
ORDER BY r.region_name, t.trust_name, s.specialty_name;


 
 Q6. Subquery — Trusts with above-average total waiting lists
 
 Business question: Which trusts have a total waiting list size
 above the national average across all snapshots?
 Flags trusts that may be under-resourced relative to peers.

SELECT t.trust_name,
       t.trust_code,
       r.region_name,
       SUM(w.total_waiting) AS trust_total_waiting
FROM   Waiting_List_Snapshot w
JOIN   Trust  t ON w.trust_id  = t.trust_id
JOIN   Region r ON t.region_id = r.region_id
GROUP BY t.trust_id, t.trust_name, t.trust_code, r.region_name
HAVING SUM(w.total_waiting) > (
    SELECT AVG(trust_sum)
    FROM (
        SELECT SUM(total_waiting) AS trust_sum
        FROM   Waiting_List_Snapshot
        GROUP BY trust_id
    )
)
ORDER BY trust_total_waiting DESC;


 
 Q7. GROUP BY with HAVING — Specialties with >500 breaching patients
 
 Business question: Which specialties have more than 500 patients
 collectively breaching the 18-week standard?
 Drives elective recovery planning targets.

SELECT s.specialty_name,
       SUM(p.patient_count) AS total_breach_patients
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
WHERE  p.is_breach = 1
GROUP BY s.specialty_name
HAVING SUM(p.patient_count) > 500
ORDER BY total_breach_patients DESC;


 
 Q8. Aggregate with ratio — Breach rate per trust
 
 Business question: What percentage of each trust's pathway records
 are in breach of the 18-week standard?
 Calculates a performance KPI comparable to NHS England's RTT dashboard.

SELECT t.trust_name,
       COUNT(*)                                                        AS total_pathways,
       SUM(p.is_breach)                                               AS breaching_pathways,
       ROUND(100.0 * SUM(p.is_breach) / COUNT(*), 1)                 AS breach_rate_pct,
       SUM(p.patient_count)                                           AS total_patients,
       SUM(CASE WHEN p.is_breach = 1 THEN p.patient_count ELSE 0 END) AS breach_patients
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Trust t ON p.trust_id = t.trust_id
GROUP BY t.trust_id, t.trust_name
ORDER BY breach_rate_pct DESC;


 
 Q9. Correlated subquery — Most pressured specialty per trust
 
 Business question: For each trust, which specialty has the longest
 maximum waiting time?
 Identifies the single biggest pressure point for each provider.

SELECT t.trust_name,
       s.specialty_name,
       p.weeks_waiting AS max_weeks_waiting
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Trust     t ON p.trust_id     = t.trust_id
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
WHERE  p.weeks_waiting = (
    SELECT MAX(p2.weeks_waiting)
    FROM   Patient_Pathway p2
    WHERE  p2.trust_id = p.trust_id
)
ORDER BY max_weeks_waiting DESC;


 
 Q10. Multi-level aggregation — Department-level summary
 
 Business question: Comparing Surgical vs Medical departments,
 which carries a higher total patient burden and breach volume?
 Supports directorate-level resource allocation decisions.

SELECT s.department,
       COUNT(DISTINCT s.specialty_id)                                  AS specialties_count,
       SUM(p.patient_count)                                            AS total_patients,
       SUM(CASE WHEN p.is_breach = 1 THEN p.patient_count ELSE 0 END) AS breach_patients,
       ROUND(
           100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN p.is_breach = 1 THEN p.patient_count ELSE 0 END)
           / NULLIF(SUM(p.patient_count), 0),
       1)                                                              AS breach_rate_pct
FROM   Patient_Pathway p
JOIN   Specialty s ON p.specialty_id = s.specialty_id
GROUP BY s.department
ORDER BY total_patients DESC;
